1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,120
Good evening everyone. My name's Phil Sutton

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,537
and I'm chairman of the Highways Committee.

3
00:00:07,537 --> 00:00:15,074
We've called this meeting to inform members of the public about the new regulations for traffic

4
00:00:15,074 --> 00:00:17,900
and parking we're proposing for Granford.

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:24,600
I'll start by summarising these changes before we open the meeting to questions.

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,096
So, why do we need to make these changes to traffic systems in Granford?

7
00:00:31,096 --> 00:00:36,200
Well, we're very aware that traffic is becoming an increasing problem.

8
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,318
It's been especially noticeable with the increase in heavy traffic

9
00:00:40,318 --> 00:00:43,200
while they've been building the new hospital.

10
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:49,600
But it's the overall rise in the volume of traffic of all kinds that's concerning us.

11
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,600
To date there's not been any increase in traffic accidents,

12
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,600
but that's not something we want to see happen, obviously.

13
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:01,240
We recently carried out a survey of local residents

14
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:04,800
and their responses were interesting.

15
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:13,300
People were very concerned about the lack of visibility on some roads due to cars parked along the sides of the roads.

16
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,153
We'd expected complaints about the congestion near the school

17
00:01:17,174 --> 00:01:21,027
when parents are dropping off their children or picking them up

18
00:01:21,027 --> 00:01:23,732
but this wasn't top of the list,

19
00:01:23,732 --> 00:01:26,980
and nor were noise and fumes from trucks and lorries

20
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:30,300
though they were mentioned by some people.

21
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:35,020
We think these new traffic regulations would make a lot of difference

22
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:38,500
But we still have a long way to go.

23
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,480
We've managed to keep our proposals within budget

24
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,602
just, so they can be covered by the Council.

25
00:01:44,602 --> 00:01:48,821
But, of course, it's no good introducing new regulations

26
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:52,498
if we don't have a way of making sure that everyone obeys them

27
00:01:52,498 --> 00:01:58,600
and that's an area we're still working on with the help of representatives from the police force.

28
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:04,200
OK, so this slide shows a map of the central area of Granford,

29
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:09,800
with the High Street in the middle and School Road on the right.

30
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:16,513
Now, we already have a set of traffic lights in the High Street at the junction with Station Road,

31
00:02:16,513 --> 00:02:20,400
but we're planning to have another set at the other end,

32
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:25,700
at the School Road junction, to regulate the flow of traffic along the High Street.

33
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:30,700
We've decided we definitely need a pedestrian crossing.

34
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,230
We considered putting this on School Road,

35
00:02:33,230 --> 00:02:40,095
just outside the school, but in the end we decided that could lead to a lot of traffic congestion

36
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:42,780
so we decided to locate it on the High Street

37
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:46,600
crossing the road in front of the supermarket.

38
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:50,300
That's a very busy area, so it should help things there.

39
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,846
We're proposing some changes to parking.

40
00:02:52,846 --> 00:02:59,460
At present, parking isn't allowed on the High Street outside the library

41
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,485
but we're going to change that,

42
00:03:00,485 --> 00:03:07,700
and allow parking there, but not at the other end of the High Street near School Road.

43
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:11,773
There'll be a new 'No Parking' sign on School Road,

44
00:03:11,773 --> 00:03:16,661
just by the entrance to the school, forbidding parking for 25 metres.

45
00:03:16,661 --> 00:03:19,920
This should improve visibility for drivers and pedestrians,

46
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:24,400
especially on the bend just to the north of the school.

47
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,559
As far as disabled drivers are concerned,

48
00:03:27,559 --> 00:03:31,120
at present they have parking outside the supermarket

49
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,878
but lorries also use those spaces,

50
00:03:33,878 --> 00:03:41,100
so we've got two new disabled parking spaces on the side road up towards the bank.

51
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:45,800
It's not ideal, but probably better than the present arrangement.

52
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:50,500
We also plan to widen the pavement on School Road.

53
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:55,981
We think we can manage to get an extra half-metre on the bend just before you get to the school,

54
00:03:55,981 --> 00:03:57,900
on the same side of the road.

55
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:01,860
Finally, we've introduced new restrictions on loading

56
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,550
and unloading for the supermarket,

57
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:09,200
so lorries will only be allowed to stop there before 8 am.

58
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,740
That's the supermarket on School Road

59
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:17,300
we kept to the existing arrangements with the High Street supermarket.
